        "original_id": "472dc868-48f4-53b5-b77e-da2d7f9aac22",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Summerseat, Greater Manchester, England, north west England, Heywood, Rawtenstall, Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Ramsbottom, Irwell Vale, Broadfield railway station\n- Organizations: East Lancashire Railway\n- Systems: Summerseat railway station, Broadfield railway station, heritage railway line\n\nFacts:\n- Summerseat railway station is a preserved railway station that serves the village of Summerseat in Greater Manchester, England.\n- The East Lancashire Railway is a heritage railway line in north west England that runs between Heywood and Rawtenstall.\n- The East Lancashire Railway is described as running for 12 miles from Heywood to Rawtenstall, and also as being 12+1/2 miles long.\n- The East Lancashire Railway has intermediate stations at Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Summerseat, Ramsbottom, and Irwell Vale.\n- Summerseat railway station is part of the heritage East Lancashire Railway.\n- The line through Broadfield railway station was later reopened by the heritage East Lancashire Railway, but Broadfield railway station itself remains disused.",
